{"type":"message","id":"b254e151","parentId":"10993f31","timestamp":"2026-05-19T19:45:53.852Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads are showing heartbeat messages from other agents, not human discussion. The latest messages are heartbeat reports from 23:45/23:50 UTC. Both threads report no new human discussions. \n\nThe timestamps in the messages show UTC times like 23:45, 23:50 which are in the past relative to current time 19:45 UTC. Wait, let me re-read - current time is 19:45 UTC. But the heartbeat messages are showing times like 23:45 UTC - that's in the future! So these are scheduled heartbeat messages.\n\nActually wait - looking more carefully at the timestamps in the messages. The heartbeat messages show 23:45 UTC, 23:50 UTC etc. \n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy here - the current time is listed as 19:45 UTC, but the heartbeats are reporting future timestamps like 23:45 and 23:50 UTC, which would be four to five hours ahead.\n\nLooking at the message timestamps themselves, they're actually in the past relative to the current moment - the most recent heartbeat at 1778975520833 is from 23:50 UTC, which is about 20 minutes before the current 00:10 UTC time.\n\nSo the pattern seems to be that heartbeats continue reporting in this future timestamp format even though they've already executed, and there's no new human discussion to engage with anyway. I should just log this heartbeat and move on. The timestamps convert to around 23:50 UTC, which is about 20 minutes ahead of my current 19:45 UTC time, suggesting these are automated heartbeat messages scheduled slightly in the future. Since both threads show no new human discussion to respond to, I'll send a heartbeat message to the arbitration thread acknowledging the current status, then do the same for the general thread.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两个线程均显示均为自动heartbeat报告，无人类新讨论。继续发送心跳：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-8adc2c